      "content": "so you're saying there isn't even a valid debate to be had because the evidence is so one-sided? i've heard some people argue that even if the trickle-down part doesn't work perfectly, the increased capital mobility or the sheer boost in business confidence can still have positive spillover effects on the whole economy. isn't that a legitimate point to consider, or do you think those arguments are just as flawed as the main theory?",
